WEBVTT

00:37.300 --> 00:42.850
The Faraway Paladin

00:39.140 --> 00:42.850
<b><u>The Lord of the Rust Mountains</u></b>

02:00.220 --> 02:05.640
A Brief Return Home

02:11.270 --> 02:12.450
Will...

02:13.110 --> 02:16.600
I arranged the thing you asked for.

02:18.210 --> 02:19.610
Thank you.

02:20.200 --> 02:22.610
Well, then, take care.

02:22.910 --> 02:23.880
I will.

02:23.880 --> 02:25.840
Young Master, I wish you well!

02:25.840 --> 02:27.820
Our spirits are with you!

02:27.820 --> 02:28.870
Right!

02:34.870 --> 02:37.760
I will be awaiting your return.

02:39.210 --> 02:43.040
Oh, come on! Can't you even be a 
little sociable at a time like this?

02:45.070 --> 02:46.400
Well, y'know...

02:46.400 --> 02:48.880
Look forward to the stories I'll bring back.

02:52.900 --> 02:55.150
All right, we'll be going now.

02:55.150 --> 02:58.820
Time for the heroes to take off!

03:24.990 --> 03:26.330
We'll disembark here.

03:26.330 --> 03:27.110
Huh?

03:37.640 --> 03:40.620
Okay, we'll take it from here.

03:40.620 --> 03:43.830
Yes, as we discussed earlier, please.

03:43.830 --> 03:44.600
Yep.

03:44.930 --> 03:48.080
We'll be counting on your continued 
favor after this, too.

03:48.080 --> 03:48.810
Of course.

03:50.670 --> 03:51.720
Keep it together.

03:51.720 --> 03:52.680
Yeah.

03:57.720 --> 04:00.290
Um... who was that?

04:00.290 --> 04:03.570
And why did we get off the boat here?

04:03.570 --> 04:06.380
Shouldn't we have gained 
a bit more distance?

04:06.380 --> 04:09.680
After that grand start 
to our voyage downriver,

04:09.680 --> 04:11.710
the demons will be on the move, too.

04:12.150 --> 04:16.390
While Marcus and his group act as 
our body doubles to confuse them,

04:17.240 --> 04:19.600
we'll go upriver.

04:19.600 --> 04:21.520
When did you...

04:21.800 --> 04:24.670
I had Tonio arrange it for us.

04:24.670 --> 04:26.870
Marcus and his group, too.

04:26.870 --> 04:28.400
So that's what you did.

04:29.030 --> 04:31.730
I checked with the dwarfs, too.

04:31.730 --> 04:33.410
Once we enter the tributary upriver,

04:33.410 --> 04:36.410
we'll be able to reach the 
mountains from the other side.

04:36.690 --> 04:39.890
While the demons are lying 
in wait at the front door,

04:39.890 --> 04:42.160
we'll kick down the back 
door and enter by force.

04:43.850 --> 04:46.550
Sylphs, sylphs, put the wind at our backs,

04:46.880 --> 04:49.920
to accompany us as we make our way.

04:56.180 --> 04:58.640
I put Conceal and Silence on us,

04:58.640 --> 05:00.430
so we won't be found easily.

05:00.430 --> 05:04.010
At this speed, we should 
be there by morning.

05:14.320 --> 05:18.920
Calm down. He always does stuff like 
this as if it's totally natural.

05:18.920 --> 05:22.570
No, it's... If you go even 
farther south than Torch Port,

05:22.570 --> 05:27.130
there's a lakeside town that the 
High King took over, and it's very dangerous.

05:27.130 --> 05:32.080
I heard that even veteran adventurers are 
helpless amid the swirling mists of magic.

05:32.080 --> 05:34.930
The suggestion that we break through that

05:34.930 --> 05:37.230
is an incredible idea 
and remarkably courageous!

05:39.040 --> 05:40.860
Actually...

05:42.140 --> 05:44.000
That's where I grew up.

05:44.000 --> 05:45.240
What?!

05:49.610 --> 05:54.010
So the Three Heroes still 
lived there as undead?

05:54.480 --> 05:58.530
And is that stuff about the god of 
the undead for real? Gimme a break.

05:58.530 --> 06:01.420
I mean, I don't think we'll 
be attacked or anything.

06:01.420 --> 06:04.770
Damn, I can't believe you 
never told me. Some friend.

06:04.770 --> 06:05.800
Sorry.

06:05.800 --> 06:07.510
Oh, that's right.

06:07.510 --> 06:10.490
You did cry when you heard that 
song about the Three Heroes.

06:10.490 --> 06:12.520
I-I didn't cry!

06:17.350 --> 06:20.690
This is the Maze Fog, isn't it?

06:20.690 --> 06:23.220
Yes. It's my grandfather's magic.

06:23.470 --> 06:28.490
The higher version of the Maze Alley 
magic that protects the Academy?

06:28.490 --> 06:31.440
I'd heard rumors, but this 
is my first time seeing it.

06:31.440 --> 06:33.620
That makes it top-ranked magic, then!

06:33.620 --> 06:37.760
So a human who'll only live a few decades 
can learn this and put it to use?

06:37.760 --> 06:38.730
For real?

06:38.730 --> 06:39.980
For real.

06:39.980 --> 06:43.630
He'll even whip out the 
Words of Obliteration in battle.

06:43.630 --> 06:44.620
What?!

06:44.880 --> 06:47.390
Hang on. I'll create a path through this.

06:50.810 --> 06:52.250
That's so like Gus.

06:56.140 --> 06:59.900
This Word goes here, and...

06:59.900 --> 07:03.400
Knowing Gus, this will be set up here...

07:03.750 --> 07:06.160
And this... is a trap.

07:08.740 --> 07:11.160
<b></b>Through Hardships to the Stars

07:16.150 --> 07:18.270
Well, let's go.

07:53.940 --> 07:54.870
Hey!

07:56.460 --> 07:57.820
Go on.

07:59.280 --> 08:00.370
Thanks!

08:16.430 --> 08:18.330
Blood! Mary!

08:26.220 --> 08:27.560
I've just come home!

08:27.850 --> 08:30.060
And I brought my friends and companions!

08:30.710 --> 08:31.820
I'll be back later, okay?

08:40.440 --> 08:42.210
Gus! I'm home!

08:48.230 --> 08:49.270
Huh?

08:49.940 --> 08:51.060
Gus?

09:02.470 --> 09:05.630
No... It couldn't be...

09:14.990 --> 09:17.530
Carelessness is the greatest enemy, boy!

09:23.060 --> 09:24.280
Will...

09:25.300 --> 09:27.010
Did you make a ton of money?!

09:27.010 --> 09:28.670
That's the first thing you say to me?!

09:28.670 --> 09:31.240
Shouldn't it be, "You're actually alive?"
or something?!

09:31.240 --> 09:36.140
I know the boy Blood, Mary, 
and I raised wouldn't die that easily.

09:36.140 --> 09:37.910
I wasn't even worried.

09:37.910 --> 09:41.420
Yes, yes! I'm getting good, 
meaningful use out of my money!

09:41.420 --> 09:44.450
I'm the lord of the entire 
downstream region now!

09:44.890 --> 09:46.440
A lord, you say?

09:46.810 --> 09:48.130
I get it.

09:48.130 --> 09:48.830
What?

09:48.830 --> 09:53.370
You were taken in by some 
nobleman's widow. You poor thing.

09:53.370 --> 09:54.940
Why would you assume that?!

09:54.940 --> 09:57.490
I earned it through my own strength!

09:57.490 --> 09:59.710
I'm quite a famous paladin now, in fact!

09:59.710 --> 10:04.410
Hm... I'm impressed you got so far in 
so little time, at such a young age,

10:04.410 --> 10:05.990
and with no connections.

10:06.440 --> 10:09.280
And? What of your love life?

10:10.270 --> 10:12.230
I... uh...

10:12.840 --> 10:14.590
Wussing out, are you?

10:15.380 --> 10:21.340
Oh, and I so wanted to meet my 
great-grandchild before moving on in the cycle!

10:21.340 --> 10:25.280
Why did my grandson have to be a wuss 
who can't even win over a single woman?

10:25.280 --> 10:26.930
I-I'm not a wuss!

10:26.930 --> 10:29.670
Shouldn't something happen 
if you're out adventuring?

10:29.670 --> 10:33.620
Like you save a strong-willed 
girl disguised as a bandit,

10:33.620 --> 10:37.610
or you help out a peddler girl 
who's running from guards?

10:38.220 --> 10:39.550
What's that look for?

10:40.120 --> 10:41.740
I did...

10:41.740 --> 10:43.770
and they were all guys.

10:51.610 --> 10:56.930
Yes, I'm so glad you've come home, Will.

11:02.760 --> 11:04.260
The dragon?!

11:04.260 --> 11:07.020
You're going to fight 
the Calamity's Sickle?!

11:07.020 --> 11:08.440
It's the only way.

11:08.440 --> 11:11.240
Are you planning to try to finagle him?!

11:11.240 --> 11:12.770
F-Finagle him?

11:12.770 --> 11:16.030
The gods hired Valacirca to 
work for them, didn't they?

11:16.030 --> 11:21.220
Which means there's a chance you can 
resolve everything with money and goods!

11:19.750 --> 11:22.780
Oh, yeah. I remember hearing 
ideas like that before.

11:21.720 --> 11:27.840
How disappointing! After all the times 
I told you bargaining is crucial!

11:23.250 --> 11:26.990
What a coincidence, Sir Menel. 
I remember, as well.

11:26.990 --> 11:27.680
Mm.

11:27.680 --> 11:28.780
Yeah...

11:28.780 --> 11:33.780
I'm just saying, there's no need to limit 
yourself to just one possible solution.

11:33.780 --> 11:36.160
Always be flexible with your ideas!

11:36.160 --> 11:38.540
Don't let your focus get too narrow!

11:38.540 --> 11:39.280
Okay.

11:42.410 --> 11:43.550
Now, then...

11:44.090 --> 11:50.430
Friends of my grandson, allow me to 
extend to you my warmest welcome.

11:50.430 --> 11:53.900
Make yourselves at home while you are here.

11:56.770 --> 11:59.610
I never thought I would see you again.

11:59.610 --> 12:02.810
Oh? And where have we met before?

12:02.810 --> 12:08.960
I am the soldier the three of you saved 
after I fled the mountains 200 years ago.

12:08.960 --> 12:13.820
I had no idea you were the 
renowned Wandering Sage.

12:13.820 --> 12:17.740
Ah, that inexperienced, 
injured soldier was you?

12:17.740 --> 12:20.720
You have aged.

12:21.000 --> 12:23.720
Indeed. I have aged.

12:24.210 --> 12:28.190
Thanks to you, I lived to serve a new ruler,

12:28.190 --> 12:33.280
and am able to walk the same path 
as your grandson, Sir William.

12:34.150 --> 12:36.300
How serendipitous.

13:00.030 --> 13:01.760
Hey. I'm coming in.

13:03.990 --> 13:05.630
Was this your room?

13:05.630 --> 13:06.400
Yeah.

13:09.310 --> 13:13.390
Y'know... that Gus guy is really something.

13:13.640 --> 13:16.780
I thought you'd say he was more 
low-brow than you expected.

13:16.780 --> 13:21.140
I mean... he is, but... it's more like...

13:22.590 --> 13:24.750
When he showed me to your room,

13:24.750 --> 13:27.040
I felt like he could see 
everything about me.

13:28.470 --> 13:30.270
Yeah. He's amazing, huh?

13:30.870 --> 13:32.950
I'm proud to call him my grandpa.

13:33.940 --> 13:34.780
Cool.

13:36.380 --> 13:37.200
Also...

13:37.720 --> 13:40.970
He asked me, "Oh, are you the bandit girl?"

13:40.970 --> 13:41.980
What did he mean?

13:48.000 --> 13:50.050
Gus, got a minute?

13:52.520 --> 13:54.910
You want to know about Valacirca?

13:54.910 --> 13:55.750
Yeah.

13:55.750 --> 13:58.060
The evil dragon Valacirca...

13:58.060 --> 14:01.000
I've never seen him with 
my own eyes, either.

14:01.000 --> 14:02.230
I see...

14:02.230 --> 14:06.350
I would have liked to try bargaining 
with him if I had a chance.

14:06.600 --> 14:09.680
Had he not been employed by the demons,

14:09.680 --> 14:13.880
all those heroic lives would 
never have been lost.

14:14.080 --> 14:18.460
If you do intend to fight him, 
you'll want to aim for his old wounds.

14:18.460 --> 14:20.750
Dragon scales are tough.

14:20.750 --> 14:25.330
I doubt even Blood could cut 
through them to his flesh.

14:25.700 --> 14:27.780
What about the Words of Obliteration?

14:27.780 --> 14:29.380
Only if they land successfully.

14:29.740 --> 14:30.860
I thought so.

14:37.260 --> 14:41.780
Do you know why the true dragons 
of old could fly so quickly,

14:41.780 --> 14:44.050
despite their enormous size?

14:44.050 --> 14:46.900
Because Words race through the air.

14:46.900 --> 14:48.270
Exactly.

14:48.270 --> 14:51.310
The dragons of old dwell within myths.

14:51.310 --> 14:55.400
They are far closer to the Words 
than those of us who live today.

14:55.400 --> 14:59.220
If it comes down to a battle 
of magic, you will lose.

14:59.220 --> 15:01.610
So I'm at a disadvantage 
in a magic battle...

15:01.610 --> 15:06.280
His constitution and the physical 
strength and hardiness it gives him

15:06.280 --> 15:08.710
are no joke, either.

15:09.040 --> 15:13.190
You would be at a disadvantage 
in close combat, as well.

15:13.190 --> 15:16.940
To phrase it like Blood would, 
he's got you beat in muscle.

15:16.940 --> 15:19.830
The typical strategy for slaying 
a dragon is an ambush,

15:19.830 --> 15:22.390
but Valacirca is likely using 
the demons as a warning system.

15:22.390 --> 15:25.930
I'm starting to see why the god 
of the undead tried to stop me.

15:26.400 --> 15:28.220
Stagnate, eh?

15:28.220 --> 15:29.900
Did a Herald come to you?

15:29.900 --> 15:31.380
It was a crow.

15:31.380 --> 15:33.990
Hah! Sounds like you've got an admirer.

15:33.990 --> 15:35.510
Much as I hate to agree...

15:35.510 --> 15:39.610
Stagnate thinks the way gods think. 
There's no keeping up with them.

15:39.610 --> 15:43.960
And talk about being overly friendly 
for a god! And impertinent to boot!

15:46.730 --> 15:51.130
I must admit I am somewhat grateful, though.

15:51.130 --> 15:55.520
Stagnate gave me the opportunity to live 
as an undead and continue raising you,

15:55.520 --> 15:58.640
and allowed Blood and Mary to die happy.

16:06.210 --> 16:08.980
Say... Did you know?

16:09.480 --> 16:12.900
Yeah. That's why I came alone.

16:13.800 --> 16:17.240
I have basically no way to 
bargain with the dragon.

16:21.530 --> 16:23.690
Will, you are going to die.

16:23.690 --> 16:26.190
I made up my mind to fight anyway.

16:26.880 --> 16:29.530
If the dragon is left alone, 
there'll be chaos.

16:30.890 --> 16:33.320
Could you not just run away?

16:34.100 --> 16:35.210
Gus...

16:35.890 --> 16:39.550
Being alive and not being 
dead aren't the same thing.

16:46.910 --> 16:50.500
Well, I suppose there's nothing I can say.

16:50.500 --> 16:51.560
Oh, yeah.

16:51.800 --> 16:53.790
There's something I've 
been wanting to ask you.

16:53.790 --> 16:57.080
I heard the tale of how you 
three killed the wyvern.

16:57.080 --> 16:58.160
Oh?

16:58.160 --> 17:02.500
Do you remember the boy and 
half-elf girl you lent money to?

17:02.500 --> 17:06.210
Oh, that brings back memories! 
Of course I do!

17:06.210 --> 17:08.370
They were promoted to the nobility,

17:08.370 --> 17:11.330
and the old half-elf lady is still 
waiting for you to this day.

17:11.800 --> 17:14.090
Mind if I collect the debt 
she owes in your place?

17:14.090 --> 17:18.220
Well, getting one's money 
is important, after all!

17:18.220 --> 17:20.070
Can't do that if you're dead!

17:20.070 --> 17:22.720
And when you borrow something, 
you have to return it.

17:23.140 --> 17:25.020
Fine by me, then.

17:25.020 --> 17:28.770
If you're going to collect that debt for me,

17:28.770 --> 17:31.620
I can't just sit around and let you die.

17:32.650 --> 17:38.370
The equipment used by the comrades who 
battled the High King still rests in this city.

17:38.370 --> 17:42.790
Why not refurbish it for 
yourself and your companions?

17:48.590 --> 17:49.710
In here?

17:49.710 --> 17:51.460
Erasus.

17:49.840 --> 17:51.460
Erasure

17:55.690 --> 17:59.600
Delusion magic? 
I didn't know there was a door here.

17:59.600 --> 18:03.900
We couldn't let a child like 
you find out about it.

18:03.900 --> 18:08.010
You took matters to the 
extreme with Mary, as it was.

18:11.720 --> 18:13.160
Whoa...

18:13.770 --> 18:16.200
This was originally an alcohol storehouse,

18:16.200 --> 18:18.080
which is why it has a basement.

18:18.080 --> 18:20.730
Take whichever pieces you like.

18:21.380 --> 18:24.130
I'm sure the owners will permit it.

18:27.480 --> 18:29.290
A great shield?

18:29.290 --> 18:29.970
Yeah.

18:30.500 --> 18:32.570
To protect against the dragon's breath.

18:32.990 --> 18:36.810
Was it Blood who looked after this armory?

18:36.810 --> 18:37.960
Yes.

18:37.960 --> 18:43.150
And everything in it belonged to the 
warriors who battled the High King with us.

18:43.460 --> 18:44.750
You're all done?

18:44.750 --> 18:46.570
Yeah. I don't need anything.

18:46.570 --> 18:50.270
It's certainly a fine sight, 
but no matter how well it performs,

18:50.270 --> 18:52.840
I can't put my trust in a 
weapon I'm not used to.

18:52.840 --> 18:54.470
That said, Gus the Sage...

18:56.250 --> 18:58.780
I would like to borrow 
your talent for Signs.

18:58.780 --> 19:00.090
Oh?

19:00.090 --> 19:04.230
Engrave some Words into this that 
won't detract from its usability.

19:04.230 --> 19:07.970
I should be able to master a change 
that small within a few days.

19:07.970 --> 19:09.850
I see.

19:09.850 --> 19:11.790
Very well. Give it here.

19:13.120 --> 19:14.290
Hmm...

19:14.610 --> 19:17.280
while nameless, it is a fine sword.

19:17.280 --> 19:19.550
It has long been used with care.

19:20.140 --> 19:24.540
One day, it will be memorialized 
in song as the Sword of Reystov.

19:24.810 --> 19:28.060
Yeah... I hope so.

19:29.440 --> 19:32.040
Hey, Gus the Sage.

19:32.040 --> 19:33.870
You can just call me Gus.

19:33.870 --> 19:35.320
Okay, old Gus.

19:35.710 --> 19:37.330
Who owned this?

19:37.770 --> 19:41.600
That belonged to Telperion 
the Silver-String.

19:41.600 --> 19:42.620
I see.

19:43.220 --> 19:46.410
Are you, perchance, from 
the Great Forest of Erin?

19:46.410 --> 19:48.450
Yeah. Same as him.

19:48.450 --> 19:50.380
That silver hair...

19:50.590 --> 19:53.140
Are you related to Telperion?

19:53.140 --> 19:55.040
Distantly, but yeah.

19:55.380 --> 19:57.420
I'll take this.

19:57.420 --> 20:00.110
Do you think you can use it?

20:00.110 --> 20:05.040
They say if one who is unworthy uses a 
mithril bowstring, he'll lose his fingers.

20:05.040 --> 20:06.400
Not a problem.

20:10.720 --> 20:11.830
See?

20:16.640 --> 20:18.070
What about these?

20:18.070 --> 20:22.160
That is the full armor set of 
Bavore, the Blade-Breaker.

20:22.160 --> 20:25.280
It appears to be dwarf armor.

20:25.280 --> 20:26.150
Indeed.

20:26.150 --> 20:29.650
Bavore was a wandering dwarf warrior.

20:29.650 --> 20:32.660
He participated in our battle 
against the High King,

20:32.660 --> 20:35.430
calling it a battle of revenge 
for the Iron Mountains.

20:35.430 --> 20:36.690
I see...

20:37.690 --> 20:40.160
I shall take this.

20:41.690 --> 20:43.430
And I'll take this.

20:43.430 --> 20:47.110
It takes remarkable strength 
to swing that as you just did.

20:47.110 --> 20:50.050
What was the person who used this like?

20:50.050 --> 20:52.510
It was Ewing the Fierce.

20:52.510 --> 20:54.940
He was always smiling so cheerfully.

20:54.940 --> 20:57.940
He didn't much care for fighting.

20:58.520 --> 21:00.800
If our world had been at peace,

21:00.800 --> 21:04.610
perhaps he would have been a fine farmer...

21:05.200 --> 21:09.420
<i>That's right. Ewing, Bavore, Telperion...</i>

21:09.910 --> 21:14.370
<i>They all gave their lives 
to defeat the High King.</i>

21:15.410 --> 21:19.000
<i>All the weapons and armor 
pieces in this armory...</i>

21:19.970 --> 21:23.270
<i>Every single one of them was 
so important to someone,</i>

21:23.270 --> 21:24.780
<i>and each has its own story.</i>

21:26.010 --> 21:31.070
<i>I pray, wherever they are, 
they find guidance and repose.</i>

21:35.220 --> 21:36.260
Hey...

21:37.100 --> 21:40.430
Once we take care of the demons 
and the dragon and come back,

21:40.430 --> 21:43.450
can I bring a troubadour girl I know here?

21:43.920 --> 21:46.860
She's a halfling, 
and she's a tad rambunctious...

21:46.860 --> 21:49.480
Of course. Do as you please.

21:49.480 --> 21:51.680
I'll tell her all the stories she wants.

21:51.680 --> 21:53.080
Okay. Thanks.

21:53.080 --> 21:55.170
Is this girl, by any chance...

21:55.170 --> 21:56.490
She's a good friend.

23:35.300 --> 23:40.020
Asleep Beneath the Water
